      "type": "text_block",
      "page": 2,
      "text": "3. A university office is preparing to scan and store three documents: a black-and-white attendance sheet, a\ncolored event photo, and a student's ID card scan. The university authority has decided to prepare a report\nfor technical specifications and future reusability, the report should i) explain the different types of digital\nimages that may correspond to the files described above, ii) explain the technique used for representing\ndigital images in computers, and iii) state the commonly used digital image formats suitable for storing and\nprocessing each of the above files. Write and prepare the report for the university. [CO1, C2, PO1 \u2014 8 + 10\n+ 7 = 25 marks]",
      "bbox": [
        56.4,
        48.41,
        555.6,
        152.92
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text_block",
      "page": 2,
      "text": "4. Digital Image Processing consists of five fundamental steps: Image Formation, Image Acquisition, Image\nTransformation, Feature Selection, and Classification. Briefly explain the core principles of Image\nTransformation and Feature Selection, and analyze the commonly used techniques and their applications in\nenhancing image analysis, pattern recognition, and classification tasks associated with these two steps.\n[CO1, C2, PO1 \u2014 10 + 15 = 25 marks]",
      "bbox": [
